# Command: MW (Set frame)
# Radio: Kenwood TS-590S / TS-590SG
# Title (cover, verbatim): "TS-590S TS-590SG / PC CONTROL COMMAND / Reference Guide"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries only "JVCKENWOOD Corporation" and
#   "January/30/2019".  ("rev3" appears only in the supplied filename.)
# Source page: printed folio "- 19 -"  ==  PDF page 20 of 35
# Chart used: the single "Set" chart of the MW block (MW has NO Read and NO Answer
#   chart in this book - only "Set" is printed)
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTH (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler):
#   MW Set = 50 positions  (five ruler rows: 1-10, 11-20, 21-30, 31-40, 41-50)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SET CHART, position by position (printed cell contents):
#   1  M          2  W
#   3  P1
#   4  P2         5-6  P3
#   7-17  P4      (11 positions)
#   18  P5
#   19  P6
#   20  P7
#   21-22  P8
#   23-24  P9
#   25-27  P10
#   28  P11
#   29  P12
#   30-38  P13   (9 positions)
#   39-40  P14
#   41  P15
#   42-49  P16   (8 positions)
#   50  ;
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGEND TEXT, VERBATIM ("[TS-590S / TS-590SG common]" / "Parameters:"):
#
# P1
#   0:  Simplex
#   1:  Split
#   * When registering a simplex channel, set parameter P1 to 0.
#     After setting P1 to 0, the channel becomes a simplex channel,
#     even if it was already a split channel.
#   * When registering a split channel, set parameter P1 to 1 (set the
#     transmission frequency and mode).  The reception frequency
#     and mode are not updated at this time.
#   * When registering a section defined channel, set parameter P1
#     to 0 to enter the Start frequency, then set P1 to 1 to set the End
#     frequency.
#   * When you have a blank channel selected, and set parameter
#     P1 to 1, the channel becomes a split channel.  However, the
#     transmit and receive frequencies are the same, and the transmit
#     and receive modes are the same.
#   * When registering a section defined channel and parameter P1
#     is set to 1, the Start and End frequencies are the same.
# P2, P3
#   Channel number (refer to the MC command)
# P4
#   Frequency (depending on the P1 setting, unused high-end
#   digits will become 0)
# P5
#   Mode (depending on the P1 setting, refer to the MD command)
# P6
#   Data mode (depending on the P1 setting, refer to the DA
#   command)
# P7
#   0:  TONE/CTCSS OFF
#   1:  TONE ON
#   2:  CTCSS ON
#   3:  Cross Tone ON
# P8
#   Tone frequency (refer to the TN command)
# P9
#   CTCSS frequency (refer to the CN command)
# P10
#   000:  Always 000
# P11 (Selected status of FILTER A/B (Status of FILTER A/B in the
#      mode indicated by P5 and P6 parameters))
#   0:  FILTER A
#   1:  FILTER B
#   This is always set to "0" in the firmware version 1.xx of TS-590S.
# P12
#   0:  Always 0
# P13
#   000000000:  Always 000000000
# P14
#   00:  FM Normal
#   01:  FM Narrow
# P15
#   0:  Channel Lockout OFF
#   1:  Channel Lockout ON
# P16
#   Memory name (up to 8 digits)
#   * ";" (semicolon) cannot be used for the parameter P16.
#
# WHAT THE BOOK SAYS ABOUT OMITTING THE NAME / SENDING A SHORTER FRAME, VERBATIM,
# AND WHAT HAPPENS TO THE CHANNEL THEN (the only such statement in the MW block):
#   "If you do not specify one digit in P16 and execute all the
#    parameters from P4 to P15 set to 0, the channels specified by
#    P2 and P3 will be erased."
#   (Nothing else is printed about shorter frames.  Nothing is printed about how a
#    1..7 character name occupies the 8 printed positions.)
#
# EVERY POSITION THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always" (by position number):
#   positions 25,26,27  (P10)  -- "000:  Always 000"
#   position  29        (P12)  -- "0:  Always 0"
#   positions 30..38    (P13)  -- "000000000:  Always 000000000"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#
#   [B1] pos 4 (P2, the 100's digit) for a channel below 100.  MC's legend permits
#        EITHER for a setting command: "When entering a setting command, enter 0 or a
#        space for a channel number less than 100."  ASSUMED: ASCII "0" below.
#   [B2] positions 7..17 (P4) - the frequency VALUE in each vector is ASSUMED; only
#        the 11-digit Hz format is documented.
#   [B3] positions 42..49 (P16) when the name is shorter than 8.  The book says
#        NOTHING about padding (see the quoted note above - it speaks only of erasure).
#        Not exercised in the two mirror vectors below (both names are exactly 8).
#   [B4] positions 21..22 (P8) and 23..24 (P9) when the tone system is OFF -
#        ASSUMED "00"; the book prints no don't-care value.
#   [B5] The erase vector below reads "do not specify one digit in P16" as meaning
#        P16 is omitted ENTIRELY (zero characters, terminator moves to position 42).
#        The phrase is ambiguous (see FINDING F7) and this reading is ASSUMED.
#   [B6] Channel numbers, mode digits and name strings are ASSUMED illustrative
#        values; only their field widths and legends are documented.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim, terminator included)
#
# Mirrors mr590_answer_ch03_simplex_name8: ordinary simplex channel, 8-character name
mw590_set_ch03_simplex_name8	MW000300014250000200000000000000000000000DXCLUSTR;
# Mirrors mr590_answer_ch12_split_tx_tone_on: split registration, TONE ON (P8=08 ->
# 88.5 Hz), FILTER B, FM Narrow
mw590_set_ch12_split_tone_on	MW101200051500000401080000010000000000010REPEATER;
# The erase shape described by the quoted note (P4..P15 all 0, P16 omitted) - 42
# positions.  See [B5] and FINDING F7.
mw590_set_ch03_erase_no_P16	MW000300000000000000000000000000000000000;
